  "slug": "coding-rnas-generates-6c5b",
  "summary": "New portals, harmonised resources and reproducible workflows aim to make spatial and single-cell data searchable, traceable and comparable across cohorts and datasets.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is infrastructure that consolidates heterogeneous spatial and single-cell data and standardizes access, rather than new inference methods. HuBMAP Data Portal hosts 9,316 public spatial and single-cell datasets from healthy human tissues. SpaceBlocks supplies a Snakemake workflow for reproducible, expert-supervised cohort-level analysis of single-cell-resolution spatial data. TRACE adds traceable curation, demonstrated in a harmonised single-cell glaucoma resource. NLM-CKN links cell phenotypes from 88 datasets and 10 organs to Cell Ontology, genes, diseases and drugs, and Gene Embedding Hub standardizes 67 gene-embedding sets. PathoEvo, SENgEAR and CircaVal add domain-specific browsers. QUEST, which virtually stains H&E to predict multiplex immunofluorescence, is a modeling contribution adjacent to this thread.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-06"
}
